From: Sergio Melas <sergiomelas@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 20 Apr 2026 04:02:41 +0800
Subject: [PATCH v3] hwmon: (yogafan) Expand hardware support and refactor HAL
 logic
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Transition the driver to a Hardware Abstraction Layer (HAL) to manage
diverse Embedded Controller (EC) behaviors across different hardware
generations. This allows the RLLag filter to remain physically
consistent across 15 distinct hardware profiles.

Support is expanded to cover a broad range of Lenovo consumer laptops,
including Yoga, Legion, LOQ, IdeaPad, and ThinkBook series. Support
for legacy discrete-step ECs is introduced via linear estimation logic.
Dynamics (Tau and Slew Rate) for these profiles are derived by scaling
reference measurements from a Yoga 14cACN based on fan diameter
(assuming moment of inertia J ∝ d²).

To prevent resource conflicts with the 'lenovo-wmi-other' driver on
modern gaming models, explicit WMI GUID detection is added to the
probe sequence. The implementation uses IS_REACHABLE logic to ensure
compatibility across diverse kernel configurations.

Reported-by: kernel test robot <lkp@intel.com>
Closes: https://lore.kernel.org/oe-kbuild-all/202604180539.EuswNnjG-lkp@intel.com/
Reported-by: Sashiko AI <sashiko@bot.internal>
Suggested-by: Rong Zhang <i@rong.moe>
See: https://lore.kernel.org/all/7fa7d4dd-7b05-4af2-a8da-6e605fa91f90@roeck-us.net/
